{"meta": {"title": "CGL 2026 Tier 2 Mock 9 - Hindi", "id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "total_questions": 130, "correct_score": "1", "negative_score": "1", "timer_minutes": "120", "timer_seconds": 7200}, "questions": [{"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50001", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The bar graph shows the revenue and the expenditure (in ₹ crore) of a company from 2019 to 2024. Study the graph and answer the question.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image001.png\" width=\"384\" height=\"214\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">In how many years was the revenue of the company more than 30% above its average annual expenditure over the six years?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Average expenditure over the six years.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Total = 70 + 85 + 75 + 90 + 80 + 80 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">480</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Average = 480 ÷ 6 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹80 crore</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The cut-off.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">30% above 80 = 80 × 130/100 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹104 crore</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Compare each year's revenue with 104.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2019: 95 — no</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2020: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">110</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> — yes</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2021: 100 — no</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2022: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">120</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> — yes</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2023: 102 — no</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2024: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">115</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> — yes</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Count.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Revenue exceeds ₹104 crore in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3 years</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> (2020, 2022, 2024).</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The base is the average EXPENDITURE, read from the other set of bars — comparing with average revenue (≈ ₹107 crore) is the trap.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2018 Mains (Tier-II)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "2", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50002", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">34 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">60 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">56 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">62 cm</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle is 26 cm and its area is 120 cm². What is the perimeter of the triangle?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:3pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image002.png\" width=\"262\" height=\"137\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Let the legs be a and b.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Pythagoras: a² + b² = 26² = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">676</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Area: ½ab = 120 ⇒ ab = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">240</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — (a + b)² = a² + b² + 2ab.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(a + b)² = 676 + 480 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1,156</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">a + b = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">34 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Perimeter.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">a + b + hypotenuse = 34 + 26 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">60 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">60 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">34 cm is only the two legs — the perimeter needs the hypotenuse too. (The legs are 10 cm and 24 cm.)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CHSL 2025 Tier-I (22 Nov 2025, Shift 3)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "4", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50003", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">15 days</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9.5 days</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">16 days</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">18 days</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">10 men or 15 women can complete a piece of work in 24 days. 6 men and 9 women start the work together. After 5 days, 3 women leave. In how many more days will the remaining workers finish the work?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — convert everyone into one kind of worker.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">10 men = 15 women ⇒ 1 man = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1.5 women</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Total work in woman-days.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">15 women × 24 days = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">360 woman-days</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">First 5 days.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6 men + 9 women = 9 + 9 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">18 women</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Work done = 18 × 5 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">90 woman-days</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Left = 360 − 90 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">270 woman-days</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">After 3 women leave.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6 men + 6 women = 9 + 6 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">15 women</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Days needed = 270 ÷ 15 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">18 days</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">18 days</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Dividing the 270 woman-days by the original 18 gives 15 days — after day 5 only 15 women-equivalents remain, so the rate must be recounted.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC Selection Post Phase XIV (Graduate Level, 19 Sep 2026)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "3", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50004", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">No profit, no loss</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Gain of ₹4,500</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Loss of ₹4,500</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Loss of ₹6,000</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A dealer sold two machines for ₹97,750 each. On one he gained 15% and on the other he lost 15%. What was the overall result of the two sales?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — recover each cost price from its own selling price.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">CP = SP ÷ (1 ± rate)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Machine sold at 15% gain.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">CP₁ = 97,750 ÷ 1.15 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹85,000</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Machine sold at 15% loss.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">CP₂ = 97,750 ÷ 0.85 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹1,15,000</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Compare the totals.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Total CP = 85,000 + 1,15,000 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹2,00,000</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Total SP = 2 × 97,750 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹1,95,500</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Loss = 2,00,000 − 1,95,500 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹4,500</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Short trick.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image003.png\" width=\"527\" height=\"61\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2.25% of ₹2,00,000 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">₹4,500</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Loss of ₹4,500</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">It is never 'no profit, no loss' — the loss-making article had the larger cost, so the 15% on it weighs more.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC Selection Post Phase XIV (Matriculation Level, 24 Sep 2026)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "2", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50005", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">74</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">70</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">60</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">84</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A solid regular square pyramid has a base of side 24 cm and a slant height of 37 cm. It is melted and recast into regular triangular pyramids, each having an equilateral triangular base of side 8 cm and height 6√3 cm. How many triangular pyramids are formed?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:3pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">-</span><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image004.png\" width=\"319\" height=\"157\" alt ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — volume of any pyramid = ⅓ × base area × height; the number recast = big volume ÷ small volume.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Height of the square pyramid from its slant height.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Slant height, height and half the base side form a right triangle.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">h = √(37² − 12²) = √(1,369 − 144) = √1,225 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">35 cm</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Volume of the square pyramid.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">V = ⅓ × 24² × 35 = ⅓ × 576 × 35 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6,720 cm³</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Volume of one triangular pyramid.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image005.png\" width=\"254\" height=\"42\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">v = ⅓ × 16√3 × 6√3 = ⅓ × 288 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">96 cm³</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Number formed.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6,720 ÷ 96 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">70</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">70</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Using the slant height 37 as the height gives 74 — the volume always needs the vertical height.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2017 Mains (Tier-II)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "4", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50006", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">62 kg</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">57 kg</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">61 kg</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">59 kg</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The average weight of 40 students of a class is 52 kg. Five students whose average weight is 48 kg leave the class and 10 new students join it. The average weight of the class now becomes 54 kg. What is the average weight of the 10 new students?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — work with totals, never with averages directly.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Original total.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">40 × 52 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2,080 kg</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">After 5 students leave.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">They take away 5 × 48 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">240 kg</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Remaining total = 2,080 − 240 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1,840 kg</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> for 35 students</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">After 10 students join.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Students now = 35 + 10 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">45</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">New total = 45 × 54 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2,430 kg</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Weight brought in by the new students.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2,430 − 1,840 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">590 kg</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Average = 590 ÷ 10 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">59 kg</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">59 kg</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Ignoring the five who left gives (50 × 54 − 2,080) ÷ 10 = 62 kg — subtract the leavers before adding the joiners.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2018 Mains (Tier-II)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50007", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">7/2</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">7</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3/2</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5/2</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Simplify: </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image006.png\" width=\"420\" height=\"46\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Expand the numerator.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(sin A + cosec A)² = sin² A + 2 + cosec² A</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(cos A + sec A)² = cos² A + 2 + sec² A</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Sum = (sin² A + cos² A) + 4 + cosec² A + sec² A</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">= 1 + 4 + (1 + cot² A) + (1 + tan² A)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">= </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">7 + tan² A + cot² A</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Remove tan² A and cot² A.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Numerator = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">7</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Simplify the denominator.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(1 + tan² A)(1 − sin² A) = sec² A × cos² A = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(1 + cot² A)(1 − cos² A) = cosec² A × sin² A = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Denominator = 1 + 1 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Divide.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image007.png\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image008.png\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Each square of (sin + cosec) or (cos + sec) carries a middle term of 2, because sin A × cosec A = 1 — dropping it gives 3/2.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CHSL 2025 Tier-I (13 Nov 2025, Shift 2)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "4", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50008", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">25</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">30.5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">32</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">29.5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The observations 12, 15, 19, x, x + 6, 31, 34, 40 are arranged in ascending order and their median is 25. If the observation 19 is replaced by 33, what is the new median?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — for an even number of observations, the median is the mean of the two middle values.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">There are </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">8</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> observations, so the median is the mean of the </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4th and 5th</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Find x.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(</span><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image009.png\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2x + 6 = 50 ⇒ x = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">22</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The data: 12, 15, 19, </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">22, 28</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, 31, 34, 40</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Replace 19 by 33 and re-arrange.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">12, 15, 22, 28, 31, 33, 34, 40</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4th = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">28</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, 5th = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">31</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">New median.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671657844_image010.png\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" alt style=\"vertical-align:middle\" ></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">29.5</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Always re-arrange after a replacement — 33 jumps past 28 and 31, so the middle pair changes.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">RRB NTPC 2025-26 Graduate Level CBT-1 (27 Mar 2026, Shift 3)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50009", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">539</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">485</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1,067</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">549</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">If 16x² + 9y² = 73 and xy = 2, where x &gt; 0 and y &gt; 0, then what is the value of 64x³ + 27y³?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — treat 4x and 3y as single terms: a = 4x, b = 3y.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">a² + b² = 16x² + 9y² = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">73</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">ab = 12xy = 12 × 2 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">24</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Find a + b.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(a + b)² = a² + b² + 2ab = 73 + 48 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">121</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">a + b = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">11</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> (both positive)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Use the sum of cubes.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">= 11 × (73 − 24)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">= 11 × 49 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">539</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">539</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Use (a + b), not (a − b) — the difference here can be +5 or −5, but the sum of cubes needs only a + b = 11.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2019 Mains (Tier-II)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "2", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50010", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">144</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">145</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">128</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">162</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">If P = √(72 + √(72 + √(72 + …∞))) and Q = √(72 − √(72 − √(72 − …∞))), then what is the value of P² + Q²?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Rule — an endless root repeats itself inside, so replace the inside by the whole.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Find P.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">P = √(72 + P)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">P² = 72 + P ⇒ P² − P − 72 = 0</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(P − 9)(P + 8) = 0 ⇒ P = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">9</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> (P is positive)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Find Q.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Q = √(72 − Q)</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Q² = 72 − Q ⇒ Q² + Q − 72 = 0</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(Q + 9)(Q − 8) = 0 ⇒ Q = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">8</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The required value.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">P² + Q² = 81 + 64 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">145</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Short trick.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Split 72 into two consecutive factors: 72 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">8 × 9</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">With + inside, the value is the larger factor (9); with − inside, the smaller one (8).</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">145</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Writing P² + Q² = 72 + 72 = 144 forgets that P² = 72 + P, not 72.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:1pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">PYQ:</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> Similar question asked in </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CGL 2022 Mains (Tier-II)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> and </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">SSC CHSL 2025 Tier-I (12 Nov 2025, Shift 2)</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> with different values.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}]}